meta {
  name: Get Branch Lab Panel Member Tests
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/branch-lab-panels/{{branchLabPanelId}}/member-tests
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  branchLabPanelId: 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
}

docs {
  The member tests of one branch lab panel + its partial-billing controls, for the
  Create-Order Diagnostic Items table's expandable panel row. Returns
  `{ panelId, isAllowPartialBilling, maxTestsRemovable, members[] }` where each
  member carries the per-test display fields (`branchLabTestId`, `name`,
  `sampleName`, `sampleType`, `isFasting`, `samplePriorityType` (ROUTINE/URGENT/STAT),
  `scheduleDays`, `scheduleFrom`, `scheduleTo`, `tatMin*`/`tatMax*`), plus
  `isRemovable` (from the BranchLabPanelTest junction) and `isBillOnlyTest`, and
  the sample-popup fields `usefulFor` (Notes → "Useful For", rich-text HTML) and
  `sampleHandlingInstructions` (of the sample named by `sampleName`, read live
  from Master Data, same as the lab-test options), both nullable.
  Members are returned in the panel's own `sortOrder`.

  The frontend uses this to let a user de-select individual tests of a panel: a
  member can be de-selected only when `isAllowPartialBilling` is true, the member's
  `isRemovable` is true, and at most `maxTestsRemovable` are removed (at least one
  must remain). The chosen subset is submitted as each panel order item's
  `selectedMemberBranchLabTestIds` (empty = all members) — only those members flow
  into accession/technician; the panel's price/billing is unaffected.

  Scoped to the JWT tenant + active branch (no `branchId` in the query). 404
  `BRANCH_LAB_PANEL_NOT_FOUND` if the panel is missing/soft-deleted/other branch.
}
